{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation pushed as Gerrit change 1600 (worktree ../514d-cr-usage, commit ec6a014b19).\n\nDESIGN NOTE on AC2 ('same helper and shape as d52a'). The plan review PASSed but raised a correct advisory I verified independently: aggregate_usage() (plan_review/pass1.py) returns a NESTED payload {per_call, per_criterion, totals}, while finalize._attach_code_review_metrics folds _usage FLAT — it reads input_tokens/output_tokens/cache_read_tokens/cache_write_tokens at the TOP level of the dict (finalize.py:169-172). So a literal shape-mirror (emitting the nested aggregate as _usage) would have folded to ZERO and left the CloudWatch under-report exactly as it was. The divergence is in the two CONSUMERS: plan-review's _attach_plan_review_metrics folds the nested form; code-review's finalize folds the flat form.\n\nResolution, which honors AC2's INTENT (one helper, no second convention) while actually fixing the undercount:\n- same helper: CodeReviewBatchRunner builds one per-call record per overlay dispatch via sizing.usage_record and aggregates with aggregate_usage.\n- same payload, same place: the full nested aggregate rides on batch_plan['usage'] — the same slot plan-review uses (coverage['usage']) — so raw per-call attribution stays reconstructable.\n- the step-output _usage is that aggregate's ['totals'] (flat), i.e. what this path's consumer actually reads.\nAttribution here is whole, not split: each dispatch is a single agent call covering exactly one criterion, so plan-review's equal-split approximation never applies.\n\nRED verified before GREEN: with the emit change reverted and the new tests in place, test_finder_batch_tokens_reach_the_finalized_totals fails 'assert 1 == 131' — only the verify step's tokens counted, which IS the reported bug. After the change: 131/26/5/7, total 157.\n\nGates run in the worktree: make lint clean; make typecheck -> Success, 498 source files; pytest tests/unit -k 'code_review or batch or usage' -> 614 passed, 3 skipped. finalize.py's folding arithmetic is untouched (only its stale gap comment replaced) and the pre-existing finalize token tests in tests/unit/test_review_bot_token_metrics.py pass unmodified.\n\nNote: the new test module was created at the path recorded in file_impact, tests/unit/test_code_review_finalize.py (that file did not previously exist)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786498049163802001,"uuid":"7693b9b0-e18b-4f90-9c16-c75ff3f89538"}